MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo Dot fits my Fire TV setup by adding hands-free voice control, giving me a useful capability alongside devices I already have.",
    "The smart plug feels like a practical next step because I could use it with the Dot to control a lamp; the Alexa displays also fit my connected-home interests, though I do not need another screen now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The HD Fire TV sticks repeat a function already covered by my Fire TV Stick 4K and Fire TV television, without giving me a clear added benefit.",
    "Neither headphones nor earbuds address a current need for me, and I have not established that I use an iPhone, so the AirPods' setup convenience does not make them compelling."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Fire TV purchases seem to have been taken as a reason to recommend more streaming sticks, even though those purchases already met that need.",
    "My interest in electronics seems to have been stretched to personal audio, while my recent choices give much clearer reasons to suggest home entertainment and connected-home equipment."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "What matters is whether a device adds a useful function to my existing setup; a voice-control point is more useful to me now than another streaming stick.",
    "Several Alexa devices appeal to me as alternatives, but I would choose one Dot now rather than also buy a Flex, an older Dot, and additional displays."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my connected-home interests but missed the difference between adding useful capabilities and duplicating equipment I already have."
}
